{
  "version": 1,
  "courseId": 1362070,
  "sourceLanguage": "en",
  "targetLanguage": "zh-TW",
  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "40270566",
      "title": "React Uses A Virtual DOM - Time To Explore It!",
      "sourceHash": "1379c8f895ce87896d5dd62c43a884fbea1cca47c4a27e1698ff1c44c4998482",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 0.48,
          "end": 3.48,
          "en": "So at this point, in this section,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 3.48,
          "end": 7.86,
          "en": "we spent a lot of time understanding how component functions",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 7.86,
          "end": 10.68,
          "en": "are executed and how you can prevent that",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 10.68,
          "end": 13.2,
          "en": "under certain circumstances.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 13.2,
          "end": 15.48,
          "en": "Now, I want to take a closer look",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 15.48,
          "end": 20.07,
          "en": "at what actually happens if a component function is executed",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 20.07,
          "end": 24.69,
          "en": "and how this JSX code here ends up on the screen.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 24.69,
          "end": 28.95,
          "en": "Because of course, the first thing you might think is",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 28.95,
          "end": 31.47,
          "en": "that when a component function gets executed",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 31.47,
          "end": 34.02,
          "en": "and this JSX code gets returned",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 34.02,
          "end": 37.98,
          "en": "and this component tree gets built, in the end,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 37.98,
          "end": 41.88,
          "en": "you end up with a bunch of native HTML elements.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 41.88,
          "end": 46.2,
          "en": "If this entire component tree is in the end resolved.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 46.2,
          "end": 51.2,
          "en": "And that then this HTML code is inserted in the DOM.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 52.32,
          "end": 55.11,
          "en": "You could think that this is what's going on,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 55.11,
          "end": 58.89,
          "en": "that the HTML elements returned by all those components",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 58.89,
          "end": 61.23,
          "en": "are inserted in the DOM.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 61.23,
          "end": 65.16,
          "en": "And indeed, that is what happens if you reload the page",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 65.16,
          "end": 68.34,
          "en": "or if you visit it for the first time.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 68.34,
          "end": 70.02,
          "en": "Because if you do that,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 70.02,
          "end": 72.78,
          "en": "you essentially start with an empty page.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 72.78,
          "end": 76.86,
          "en": "Keep in mind that it's technically this index HTML file",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 76.86,
          "end": 79.59,
          "en": "that is being loaded when you visit the website",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 79.59,
          "end": 83.7,
          "en": "and this is a pretty empty page in the end.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 83.7,
          "end": 87.24,
          "en": "It just has one div and this script import.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 87.24,
          "end": 91.65,
          "en": "And indeed, it's in this div where this entire React app.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 91.65,
          "end": 96.6,
          "en": "So this component tree and the HTML code that's generated",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 96.6,
          "end": 99.15299999999999,
          "en": "by that tree will be rendered.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 100.44,
          "end": 104.28,
          "en": "That's why if you view the page source code,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 104.28,
          "end": 105.87,
          "en": "you see nothing.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 105.87,
          "end": 108.75,
          "en": "And if you instead go to the elements tab,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 108.75,
          "end": 112.443,
          "en": "you see the, well, full DOM tree here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 114.12,
          "end": 117.81,
          "en": "So yes, this was all inserted by React,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 117.81,
          "end": 121.23,
          "en": "but if you then click a button here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 121.23,
          "end": 125.43,
          "en": "this is not all recreated and reinserted",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 125.43,
          "end": 128.46,
          "en": "because that would be super inefficient.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 128.46,
          "end": 132.9,
          "en": "So just because a component function is executed again,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 132.9,
          "end": 135.33,
          "en": "like this counter component function when we click",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 135.33,
          "end": 139.89,
          "en": "one of those buttons here, just because that happens",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 139.89,
          "end": 143.91,
          "en": "does not mean that all the JSX code that's produced",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 143.91,
          "end": 148.5,
          "en": "by that component function is reinserted in the DOM.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 148.5,
          "end": 150.6,
          "en": "The old code is not thrown away",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 150.6,
          "end": 153.72,
          "en": "and replaced by new HTML code.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 153.72,
          "end": 156.54,
          "en": "And you can see that in the DevTools.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 156.54,
          "end": 161.1,
          "en": "For example, here, if I go to the counter section",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 161.1,
          "end": 163.2,
          "en": "and I expand this paragraph,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 163.2,
          "end": 165.69299999999998,
          "en": "which does include the counter value.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 166.98,
          "end": 171.27,
          "en": "If you watch this HTML code on the right here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 171.27,
          "end": 173.49,
          "en": "as I click this button here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 173.49,
          "end": 178.49,
          "en": "you see that it's just this span here that's flashing.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 179.7,
          "end": 183,
          "en": "And in the Chrome DevTools in this elements tab,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 183,
          "end": 186.6,
          "en": "these elements flash if they are changed,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 186.6,
          "end": 190.11,
          "en": "so if the DOM changed in that place.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 190.11,
          "end": 193.92,
          "en": "So put in other words, only elements that flash here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 193.92,
          "end": 196.62,
          "en": "were touched by React.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 196.62,
          "end": 200.1,
          "en": "So when I increment this value, it looks as if React",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 200.1,
          "end": 202.56,
          "en": "is only updating this span,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 202.56,
          "end": 206.04,
          "en": "is only working with that span element.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 206.04,
          "end": 210.78,
          "en": "All the other DOM elements are not touched by React.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 210.78,
          "end": 214.38,
          "en": "Even though technically, this counter component of course,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 214.38,
          "end": 218.79,
          "en": "also returns this paragraph and all of these buttons.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 218.79,
          "end": 221.37,
          "en": "Nonetheless, none of that flashes here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 221.37,
          "end": 224.13,
          "en": "which means it's not changed in any way.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 224.13,
          "end": 226.95,
          "en": "And that's the case because React works",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 226.95,
          "end": 231.45,
          "en": "with a so-called virtual DOM for finding out",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 231.45,
          "end": 235.71,
          "en": "which parts of the actual DOM should be updated.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 235.71,
          "end": 237.69,
          "en": "And it's using this virtual DOM",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 237.69,
          "end": 240.9,
          "en": "because working with such a virtual DOM,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 240.9,
          "end": 243.09,
          "en": "which lives only in memory",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 243.09,
          "end": 248.01,
          "en": "is faster than working with that real DOM here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 248.01,
          "end": 251.16,
          "en": "So how does this virtual DOM work then?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 251.16,
          "end": 255.03,
          "en": "Well, if I reload the page and the overall React app",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 255.03,
          "end": 258.81,
          "en": "starts therefore and is rendered for the first time,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 258.81,
          "end": 262.65,
          "en": "React creates that component tree and then in the end",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 262.65,
          "end": 266.16,
          "en": "derives the actual HTML code that should be rendered",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 266.16,
          "end": 268.38,
          "en": "from that component tree",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 268.38,
          "end": 272.22,
          "en": "and it then creates a virtual DOM snapshot.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 272.22,
          "end": 275.52,
          "en": "So it's not reaching out to the real DOM yet.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 275.52,
          "end": 279.69,
          "en": "Instead, it just creates a virtual representation",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 279.69,
          "end": 283.2,
          "en": "of how that real DOM should look like.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 283.2,
          "end": 286.86,
          "en": "As a next step, React then compares that",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 286.86,
          "end": 291.27,
          "en": "to that last virtual DOM snapshot it created.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 291.27,
          "end": 296.07,
          "en": "Now, if the app just started, there is no lost snapshot",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 296.07,
          "end": 300.27,
          "en": "and therefore, React of course, sees that everything changed",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 300.27,
          "end": 304.83,
          "en": "and it goes ahead to the real DOM and makes those changes,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 304.83,
          "end": 309.63,
          "en": "which means in this case, the entire virtual DOM is inserted",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 309.63,
          "end": 311.88,
          "en": "into the real DOM, into this div",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 311.88,
          "end": 314.94,
          "en": "with the idea root in this case.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 314.94,
          "end": 318.81,
          "en": "Now, when I click a button here, React in the end",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 318.81,
          "end": 321.12,
          "en": "repeats that process.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 321.12,
          "end": 324.93,
          "en": "It again creates that component tree, and of course,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 324.93,
          "end": 326.49,
          "en": "it can quickly find out",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 326.49,
          "end": 329.85,
          "en": "that only a part of that tree changed,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 329.85,
          "end": 333.84000000000003,
          "en": "that only some of those component functions were executed.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 333.84000000000003,
          "end": 336.9,
          "en": "In this case counter, and depending on",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 336.9,
          "end": 341.37,
          "en": "if you are using memo or not, also those buttons.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 341.37,
          "end": 346.29,
          "en": "And React derives the updated HTML code.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 346.29,
          "end": 350.64,
          "en": "And it then compares that code with the old code,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 350.64,
          "end": 351.84000000000003,
          "en": "you could say.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 351.84000000000003,
          "end": 356.19,
          "en": "Still only virtually, it does not compare anything",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 356.19,
          "end": 359.46,
          "en": "with the real DOM, it just compares this new",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 359.46,
          "end": 363.303,
          "en": "virtual DOM snapshot with the old virtual DOM.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 364.17,
          "end": 366.54,
          "en": "And of course, it then quickly finds out",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 366.54,
          "end": 368.61,
          "en": "which parts changed.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 368.61,
          "end": 372.3,
          "en": "And here in this case, this is only this span",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 372.3,
          "end": 375.843,
          "en": "or this text inside of the span to be precise.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 107,
          "start": 377.28,
          "end": 381.66,
          "en": "And therefore then, as a next step, React goes ahead",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 108,
          "start": 381.66,
          "end": 385.11,
          "en": "and applies those changes to the real DOM",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 109,
          "start": 385.11,
          "end": 387.51,
          "en": "and only those changes.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 110,
          "start": 387.51,
          "end": 391.23,
          "en": "So in this case, it only goes to that span in the real DOM",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 111,
          "start": 391.23,
          "end": 394.65,
          "en": "and replaces its old text with the new text",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 112,
          "start": 394.65,
          "end": 397.68,
          "en": "and it does nothing else.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 113,
          "start": 397.68,
          "end": 400.89,
          "en": "And that is super important to understand.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 114,
          "start": 400.89,
          "end": 404.25,
          "en": "Just because a component function executes",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 115,
          "start": 404.25,
          "end": 407.97,
          "en": "and it's JSX code therefore is evaluated,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 116,
          "start": 407.97,
          "end": 412.59000000000003,
          "en": "does not mean that this code is inserted or updated",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 117,
          "start": 412.59000000000003,
          "end": 414.18,
          "en": "in the real DOM,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 118,
          "start": 414.18,
          "end": 416.85,
          "en": "because all those real DOM operations",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 119,
          "start": 416.85,
          "end": 419.64,
          "en": "are quite performance intensive",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 120,
          "start": 419.64,
          "end": 423.18,
          "en": "and therefore, React does not change the real DOM",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 121,
          "start": 423.18,
          "end": 424.02,
          "en": "all the time.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 122,
          "start": 424.02,
          "end": 427.98,
          "en": "Instead, it just creates these snapshots, compares them",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 123,
          "start": 427.98,
          "end": 430.44,
          "en": "and only makes the necessary changes",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 124,
          "start": 430.44,
          "end": 432.573,
          "en": "to get to the target result.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
}